<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
    Fix order-history withdrawal column for registered customers on Hyvä.

    The base module (zwernemann/module-withdrawal) declares the column-
    header block as the generic Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template
    in its sales_order_history.xml:

        <referenceBlock name="sales.order.history.extra.column.header">
            <block class="Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template"
                   name="zwernemann.withdrawal.column.header"
                   template="Zwernemann_Withdrawal::order/history/column_header.phtml"/>
        </referenceBlock>

    This bridge's column_header.phtml then calls $block->isEnabled() on
    that block. The generic Template class has no isEnabled() method,
    so registered customers visiting /sales/order/history hit:

        Invalid method Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template\Interceptor::isEnabled

    (Luma never hit this because the upstream Luma column_header.phtml
    doesn't call isEnabled(): it renders the <th> unconditionally.
    The Hyvä bridge added an isEnabled() guard for cleaner config-
    disabled hiding but didn't change the layout XML to match.)

    The phtml's docblock references Zwernemann\Withdrawal\Block\Order\WithdrawalHeader,
    a class that doesn't exist anywhere in the base module. Looks like
    a half-finished refactor.

    Re-declare the column-header block with the existing
    Zwernemann\Withdrawal\Block\Order\WithdrawalButton class, which:
      - already has an isEnabled() method (uses the same Config service)
      - is already the block class used for the cell row in the SAME
        column (see base sales_order_history.xml)
      - keeps header + cell visibility consistent: config-disabled
        withdrawals hide both the column header and the buttons

    This avoids requiring upstream to add a new WithdrawalHeader class
    and keeps the fix contained in the bridge module where the failing
    template lives.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <referenceBlock name="zwernemann.withdrawal.column.header" remove="true"/>
        <referenceBlock name="sales.order.history.extra.column.header">
            <block class="Zwernemann\Withdrawal\Block\Order\WithdrawalButton"
                   name="zwernemann.withdrawal.column.header.hyva"
                   template="Zwernemann_Withdrawal::order/history/column_header.phtml"/>
        </referenceBlock>
    </body>
</page>
